'' =============================================================================
'' Single-Step Debugger Test Program 03 — PASM register watch
''
'' Covers Test Plan tests:
''   Test 3 — Register watch tracks changed registers; R key / click resets
''   Test 4 — Disassembly navigation, scroll, address breakpoints
''
'' PASM-only program: cog 0 boots directly into this DAT at $000, so DEBUG_MAIN
'' breaks on the FIRST instruction (entry / mov pa,#0) — no Spin interpreter or
'' coginit indirection in the way. The disassembly shows YOUR PASM immediately
'' (R-000 entry ...), not interpreter "not my code".
''
'' Behavior: Tight PASM loop that increments PA and decrements PB.
'' Expected register watch after stepping into .loop: PA ($1F6) increments from
'' 0, PB ($1F7) decrements from 100 ($64) — e.g. PA=1, PB=$63 (99) after one pass.
'' =============================================================================
CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_MAIN = 1

DAT
                org
entry           mov     pa, #0
                mov     pb, #100
.loop           add     pa, #1
                sub     pb, #1
                jmp     #.loop
